          <groundspeak:finder id="9859564">Hallzey</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP659 NSR &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Another quick stop for a cap nearby it was right next to the road thanks for the cap&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684558603">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP659 NSR&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Another cap with an amazing view.  Well, I was first stunned by the houses along this street while driving up.  Nice to see how the other half lives.  lol  Wow!  The cap itself was a quick find.  One of my few quick walk ups today.  Not very readable but there.  Once I was finished my business I took in the view for a few minutes.  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I could see Government House Park and was happy to see some empty parking spots.  :)  lol  Yeah, I was headed there next.  But first, must drink this in for a bit.  TFTBC OFTH and for bringing me here!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682022921">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="4853503">gumbyphv</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;I found BCP659 NSR.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After the last cap, I drove by some really nice houses over to this cap.  When I pulled up, there was a kid jumping on a trampoline across the street, I stepped out and went around the vehicle to see a hole in the curb.  Is that where the cap is?  Checked in the hole to see the nice cap.  Thanks for another great cap in a nice neighbourhood and with a nice view.  TFTBC  &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681706726">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="53.539417" lon="-113.550733" />
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-28T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="11091667">WillowZilla</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP659 - NSR&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I dnf'd this about a year ago, the whole neighbourhood was getting new curbs and this area was just fresh with new sod.  I think i saw the nice little nook created for the cap ... but it was completely filled with sand or something? Not sure how i could have missed it otherwise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I saw UBC geograds log of 'quick pnG' so figured i'd go do some cap hunting after work today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This was quick quick for me today :)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681528656">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-27T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="691070">UBC Geograd</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP 659- Edmonton NSR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A quick find on my way home from work. Thought I was out of luck on logging this, as the &quot;new&quot; log page showed up for me at my first attempt. Fortunately &quot;opt out&quot; brought me back to the page where logging remained an option despite my previous find on this virtual. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cap is in tough shape, but three numbers are decipherable. Thanks for another great cap- beautiful spot for this one.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
